error[SC0417]: `f` is rebound in a loop to a closure that captures its own earlier value
  --> /main/main.sol:14:17
   |
13 |           for (let i: uint256 = 0; i < 3; i = i + 1) {
14 |               f = lam (v: uint256) -> uint256 {
   |  _________________^
15 | |                 return f(v) + 1;
16 | |             };
   | |_____________^ this closure captures a closure that the loop rebinds
17 |           }
   |
   = note: function values have no run-time representation: a value chosen by run-time control flow is compiled to a selector over a finite set of closures known at compile time
   = note: the closure captures, directly or through another variable that the loop rebinds, a closure that `f` held before, so the closures nest one level deeper with each iteration that creates it
   = note: a loop is compiled as a loop and is not unrolled, even when its trip count is known at compile time, so the closures that `f` can hold do not form a fixed set
   = note: help: keep the changing state in an ordinary variable, such as a counter or an accumulator, and build the closure from that variable instead of from a closure that the loop rebinds
